@startuml saga_architecture_overview
title SagaFlow — Visão geral da arquitetura
left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false

actor "Cliente" as Customer
component "API / Checkout" as API
component "Order Service" as Order
database "Order DB" as OrderDB
component "Saga Orchestrator\n(persistente)" as Saga
database "Saga State DB" as SagaDB
queue "Message Broker" as Broker
component "Inventory Service" as Inventory
database "Inventory DB" as InventoryDB
component "Payment Service" as Payment
database "Payment DB" as PaymentDB
cloud "Gateway financeiro" as Gateway

Customer --> API : Solicitar compra
API --> Order : Criar pedido
Order --> OrderDB : Transação local
API --> Saga : Iniciar Saga / orderId
Saga --> SagaDB : Persistir estado
Saga --> Broker : Publicar comandos
Broker --> Saga : Entregar eventos
Broker <--> Order : ConfirmOrder / CancelOrder\nOrderConfirmed / OrderCancelled
Order --> OrderDB
Broker <--> Inventory : ReserveStock / ReleaseStock\nStockReserved / StockReleased
Inventory --> InventoryDB
Broker <--> Payment : ProcessPayment\nPaymentApproved / PaymentDeclined
Payment --> PaymentDB
Payment --> Gateway : Requisição idempotente
Gateway --> Payment : Resultado

note bottom of Saga
O orquestrador coordena transações locais.
Não existe uma transação ACID global.
end note
@enduml
